= Large language model — Simple =

A '''large language model''' ('''LLM''') is a large AI model trained on huge amounts of language data so it can predict and generate text or other token sequences.

Most modern LLMs use Transformer neural networks.

An LLM is not the same thing as:

* a chatbot;
* an AI agent;
* a search engine;
* a memory system.

Those systems can use an LLM as one component.

There is also no exact number of parameters that universally defines when a language model becomes “large.”

